@@ -37,3 +37,18 @@ Throws if `patch` is not a valid JSON Patch (e.g. an operation is missing a requ
 an unknown `op`), or if applying one of its operations fails (e.g. it targets a location that does
 not exist, a `move` would relocate a value into one of its own children, or a `test` operation does
 not match).
+
+### `applyMergePatch(target, patch)`
+
+Applies a [JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386) to a JSON document and returns
+the merged document. `target` is left untouched; the result is a new value.
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: { d: 1 } }, { a: "z", c: { d: null } });
+// { a: "z", c: {} }
+```
+
+A `null` value in the patch removes the corresponding member from the target. Any non-object patch
+(including arrays) replaces the target wholesale.
